FujiNet Go Atari 5200 desktop -- milestones

[ ] M0  skeleton: staged + patched atari800 forced into 5200 mode, headless runner, boot + A/B tests, icons
[ ] M1  session without FujiNet: host thread, pacing, audio, video blits, BIOS import
[ ] M2  FujiNet cartridge: device model + planner, BoIP link to libfujinet, runtime build, auto-update pin
[ ] M3  Open / drop: cartridge images through the planner, power cycle
[ ] M4  input: 4 controllers, analog stick, keypad, START/PAUSE/RESET, gamepads
[ ] M5  debugger engine (debug_test: ASan + TSan clean) + FujiNet trace tab
[ ] M6  GNOME frontend
[ ] M7  KDE frontend
[ ] M8  Windows frontend (D3D11 display, GUI log capture)
[ ] M9  macOS frontend (CI is the first compile)
[ ] M10 packaging, CI, release (v0.1.0)

Open / unverified
  - the 5200 PAL timing and palette
  - screenshots in data/screenshots are placeholders until shot from the 5200 build
